{"name":"Mocha","hex":"#9d7651","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mocha","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village in Gujarat, India.","A village in Madhya Pradesh, India."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mocha"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mokha","blocks":[{"text":"Mokha, also spelled Mocha, is a port city on the Red Sea coast of Yemen. Until Aden and al Hudaydah eclipsed it in the 19th century, Mokha was the principal port for Yemen's capital, Sanaa. Long known for its coffee trade, the city gave its name to Mocha coffee."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Mocha_Red_Sea_-_panoramio.jpg/330px-Mocha_Red_Sea_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mokha","wikidata":"Q339258"},{"title":"Mocha Island","blocks":[{"text":"Mocha Island is a Chilean island located west of the coast of Arauco Province in the Pacific Ocean. The island is the location of numerous historic shipwrecks. In Mapuche mythology, the souls of dead people travel west to visit this island. The waters off the island are a popular place for recreational sea fishing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Isla_Mocha_1.jpg/330px-Isla_Mocha_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mocha_Island","wikidata":"Q1635008"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Mosque_and_moon_%2810632913833%29.jpg/500px-Mosque_and_moon_%2810632913833%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Mosque_and_moon_%2810632913833%29.jpg/1280px-Mosque_and_moon_%2810632913833%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Mosque_and_moon_%281